+
+## Creating a JSON Patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from`
+into `to` when passed to `applyPatch`; neither input is mutated and the patch shares no value with them.
+It describes only what changed: objects are compared member by member, and arrays are aligned on their
+longest common subsequence, so an item gained or lost is one `add` or `remove`, and a moved item a
+`remove` plus an `add`, without touching the items around it. A change of type, or of a scalar, is a
+`replace` (at path `""` for the whole document).
+
+```ts
+createPatch({ a: [1, 2, 3] }, { a: [1, 3] }); // [{ op: "remove", path: "/a/1" }]
+```
